o unhealthy. The service was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release with a healthy record. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 24421, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RqUU5VK2GPQnAME3Cdn6nR", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["await_visibility", "await_visibility", "await_visibility", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 24421, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RqUU5VK2GPQnAME3Cdn6nR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 28169, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release with a healthy record. All three regions now run it, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback and the post-rollback health. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone redeploys it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NrjmjUm2BQ1JMpDfRHRY3p", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, 